Euro-Office's own V8 change (core: Common/3dParty/v8/tools/8.9/
x64-linux-dynamic/buildgn.patch, applied there by nc-build.py), with the
paths made relative to the snapshot's top directory. V8 8.9 (2021) uses
uint8_t and friends in headers that relied on other standard headers pulling
<cstdint> in; current C++ libraries no longer do, so every V8 source gets
-include cstdint. -Wno-enum-constexpr-conversion silences what clang < 20
only warned about (later clang makes it a hard error that the flag no longer
turns off: those spots are fixed in the recipe's setup, as Euro-Office does).

diff --git a/v8/BUILD.gn b/v8/BUILD.gn
index a8618452794..4ab368a4149 100644
--- a/v8/BUILD.gn
+++ b/v8/BUILD.gn
@@ -689,6 +689,9 @@ config("toolchain") {
 
   defines = []
   cflags = []
+  if (!is_win) {
+    cflags += ["-include", "cstdint", "-Wno-enum-constexpr-conversion"]
+  }
   ldflags = []
 
   if (v8_current_cpu == "arm") {
